        "title": "Materials and Manufacturing Constraints",
        "updated": "null"
      },
      "text": "Materials and manufacturing processes are not background constraints on design -- they ARE design. The material determines possible forms; the process determines possible features; the cost model determines what can be built at scale. Ignoring these in early design is the single most common reason designs fail to reach production."
